[Ip]
Name=ADC
Version=aditf5_v1_1_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
TrigAuto|TrigAuto|ADCgroup||||
Mode|Mode|ADCs_Common_Settings||||Multi ADC mode selection: Configures the ADC to operate in independent or multi mode
DMAAccessModeView|DMA Access Mode|ADCsgroup||||
DMAAccessMode|DMA Access Mode|ADCsgroup||||
TwoSamplingDelay|Delay between 2 sampling phases|ADCsgroup||||Delay between 2 sampling phases
ChannelVREF|ChannelVREF|||||
ChannelTS|ChannelTS|||||
ChannelVBAT|ChannelVBAT|||||
FadcConstraint|Fadc Constraint|||140000|72000000|
ClockPrescaler|Clock Prescaler|ADCs_Common_Settings||||frequency of the clock to the ADC. The clock is common for all the ADCs.
Resolution|Resolution|ADCgroup||||Resolution of the ADC conversion
DataAlign|Data Alignment|ADCgroup||||Select the alignment of the data stored after conversion.
ScanConvMode|Scan Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable or Disable the Scan Conversion Mode
ContinuousConvMode|Continuous Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable or Disable the Continuous Conversion Mode
DiscontinuousConvMode|Discontinuous Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable or Disable the Discontinuous Conversion Mode
NbrOfDiscConversion|Number Of Discontinuous Conversions|ADCgroup||1|8|
DMAContinuousRequests|DMA Continuous Requests|ADCgroup||||This parameter is used only when a DMA Request is configured. Else it is not relevant. When the DMA Request for this ADC instance this parameter specifies whether the DMA requests are performed in one shot mode (DMA transfer stops when number of conversions is reached) or are performed in continuous mode (DMA transfer unlimited, whatever number of conversions). Note: In continuous mode, DMA must be configured in circular mode. Otherwise an overrun will be triggered when DMA buffer maximum pointer is reached.
EOCSelection|End Of Conversion Selection|ADCgroup||||Regular channel end of conversion selection
Overrun|Overrun behaviour|ADCgroup||||Select the behaviour in case of overrun
LowPowerAutoWait|Low Power Auto Wait|ADCgroup||||Specifies the usage of Low Power Auto Wait Mode: new conversion start only when the previous conversion (for regular group) or previous sequence (for injected group) has been treated by user software.
Rank1_Channel|Channel_Rank1|ADCChannel||||
Rank2_Channel|Channel_Rank2|ADCChannel||||
Rank3_Channel|Channel_Rank3|ADCChannel||||
Rank4_Channel|Channel_Rank4|ADCChannel||||
QueueInjectedContext|Queue Injected Context Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable/Disable the queue of injected context
EnableRegularConversion|Enable Regular Conversions|ADC_Regular_ConversionMode||||Enable/Disable Regular Conversion
NbrOfConversionFlag|Number Of Conversion Flag|ADCgroup||0|1|
NbrOfConversion|Number Of Conversion|ADCgroup||1|16|Number of regular channels to be converted
ExternalTrigConv|External Trigger Conversion Source|ADCgroup||||Select the external event used to trigger the start of conversion of a regular group
ExternalTrigConvEdge|External Trigger Conversion Edge|ADCgroup||||Select the external trigger polarity and enable the trigger of a regular group: When an external trigger is selected for ADC regular or injected conversion, only the rising edge of the signal can start the conversion.
RegHighThreshold|Regular HighThreshold|ADCChannel||||
RegLowThreshold|Regular LowThreshold|ADCChannel||||
RegITMode|Regular ITMode|ADCChannel||||
MonitoredBy|Monitored by|ADCgroup||||Select a watchdog to monitor the channel.
AWDChannel|AWDChannel|ADCChannel||||
Rank|Rank|ADCgroup||1|16|The rank in the regular group sequencer
Channel|Channel|ADCChannel||||
FHzSyncCLK|Sync Clock AHB value|||||
FHzAsyncCLK|Async Clock ADC value|||||
SamplingTime|Sampling Time|ADCChannel||||Regular Channel x sampling time selection
SamplingTimeOPAMP|Sampling Time|ADCChannel||||Regular Channel x sampling time selection with contrainst on OPAMP connection
SingleDiff|Single-ended or differential|ADCgroup||||Selection of single-ended or differential input
OffsetNumber|Offset Number|ADCgroup||||Regular Channel x offset number selection
Offset|Offset|ADCgroup||0|63|Data offset for regular channel
EnableInjectedConversion|Enable Injected Conversions|ADCgroup||||<html> <font color="red"><b>*</b>In case of usage of channels on injected group, ADC frequency should be low than AHB clock frequency /4 for resolution 12 or 10 bits, AHB clock frequency /3 for resolution 8 bits, AHB clock frequency /2 for resolution 6 bits.</font></br></html>
InjNumberOfConversion|Number Of Conversions|ADCgroup||0|4|Number of injected channels to be converted
ExternalTrigInjecConv|External Trigger Source|ADCgroup||||EXTI Line15 is used for External-Trigger-for-Injected-conversion mode
ExternalTrigInjecConvEdge|External Trigger Conversion Edge|ADCgroup||||Select the external trigger polarity and enable the trigger of a regular group: When an external trigger is selected for ADC regular or injected conversion, only the rising edge of the signal can start the conversion.
SequencerNbRanks|SequencerNbRanks|ADCgroup||||Data offset for regular channel
InjectedConvMode|Injected Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Injected Conversion Mode selection
InjectedDiscontinuousConvMode|Injected Discontinuous Conversion Mode|||||
AutoInjectedConv|Automatic Injected Conversion|||||
InjectedRank|Rank|ADCgroup||1|4|The rank in the regular group sequencer
InjectedChannel|Channel|ADCChannel||||
InjectedSamplingTime|Sampling Time|ADCChannel||||Regular Channel x sampling time selection
InjectedSamplingTimeOPAMP|Sampling Time|ADCChannel||||Regular Channel x sampling time selection with contrainst on OPAMP connection
InjectedSingleDiff|Single-ended or differential|ADCgroup||||Selection of single-ended or differential input
InjectedOffsetNumber|Offset Number|ADCgroup||||Regular Channel x offset number selection
InjMonitoredBy|Monitored by|ADCgroup||||The ADC analog input channel is not monitored by Watchdog 2 or 3.
InjHighThreshold|Injected HighThreshold|ADCChannel||||
InjLowThreshold|Injected LowThreshold|ADCChannel||||
InjITMode|Injected ITMode|ADCChannel||||
InjAWDChannel|Monitored by|ADCgroup||||
InjectedOffset|Injected Offset|ADCgroup||0|4095|Data offset for regular channel
EnableAnalogWatchDog1|Enable Analog WatchDog1 Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable/Disable Analog WatchDog1 Mode
AWD1WatchdogNumber|Watchdog instance|ADCgroup||||Number of used watchDogs.
WatchdogMode|Watchdog Mode|ADCgroup||||Configures the ADC analog watchdog mode.
WatchdogChannel|Analog WatchDog Channel|ADCChannel||||ADC channel for the analog watchdog
AWD1HighThreshold|High Threshold|ADCgroup||=AWD1LowThreshold|4095|Configures the ADC analog watchdog High threshold value.
AWD1LowThreshold|Low Threshold|ADCgroup||0|=AWD1HighThreshold|Configures the ADC analog watchdog Low threshold value.
AWD1ITMode|Interrupt Mode|ADCgroup||||Specifies whether the analog watchdog is configured in interrupt mode or in polling mode.
EnableAnalogWatchDog2|Enable Analog WatchDog2 Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable/Disable Analog WatchDog2 Mode
AWD2WatchdogNumber|Watchdog instance|ADCgroup||||Number of used watchDogs.
AWD2HighThreshold|High Threshold|ADCgroup||=AWD2LowThreshold|4095|Configures the ADC analog watchdog High threshold value.
AWD2LowThreshold|Low Threshold|ADCgroup||0|=AWD2HighThreshold|Configures the ADC analog watchdog Low threshold value.
AWD2ITMode|Interrupt Mode|ADCgroup||||Specifies whether the analog watchdog is configured in interrupt mode or in polling mode.
EnableAnalogWatchDog3|Enable Analog WatchDog3 Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable/Disable Analog WatchDog3 Mode
